   "source": [
    "# Quiz: Introduction to Reinforcement Learning and Q-Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-1-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is reinforcement learning?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>teaching someone something over and over again until they understand</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Reinforcement learning is about an agent learning the best behavior in an environment, not about teaching a person.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a learning technique that deciphers the optimal behavior of an agent in some environment by running many experiments</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Reinforcement learning finds the best behavior of an agent in an environment by running many experiments.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>understanding how to run multiple experiments at once</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Experiments are the method, not the goal. The goal is to learn the agent's best behavior.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-1-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is a policy?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a function that returns the action at any given state</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A policy is a function that returns the action at any given state.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a document that tells you whether or not you can return an item</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Here a policy is a function that picks the agent's action at each state.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a function that is used for a random purpose</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A policy has a clear job. It returns the action to take at any given state.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-1-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>A reward function returns a score for each state of an environment.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>true</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. A reward function returns a score value for each state.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>false</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A reward function does return a score value for each state.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-1-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What is Q-Learning?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>a mechanism for recording the 'goodness' of each state</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The Q-Table does record the 'goodness' of actions in each state, but it also defines the policy. Both are true.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>an algorithm where the policy is defined by a Q-Table</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. This is true, but so is the other choice. The Q-Table also records how good each action is.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>both of the above</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. In Q-Learning, a Q-Table defines the policy and records how good each action is in each state.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-1-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>For what values does a Q-Table correspond to the random walk policy?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>all equal values</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. When all Q-Table values are equal, all moves are equally good. That is the random walk policy.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>-0.25</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. The equal starting value was 0.25, not -0.25. What matters is that all the values are equal.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>all different values</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Random walk needs all moves to be equally good, so all the Q-Table values must be equal.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"mlb-quiz-8-1-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>It was better to use exploration than exploitation during the learning process in our lesson.</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>true</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Exploring at random means the agent is likely to die often. The best approach balances exploring and exploiting.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>false</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Neither one is better alone. The best approach strikes a balance between exploration and exploitation.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
